.TH PGWAL-DOCTOR 1 "2026-11-01" "pgwal-doctor 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pgwal-doctor \- read-only report of why PostgreSQL's pg_wal keeps growing
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pgwal-doctor
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read-only report of why PostgreSQL's pg_wal keeps growing.
.PP
There are no subcommands.
Offline checks read a data directory given with
.BR --datadir .
Online checks run through
.I psql
when
.B --dsn
or
.B --online
is set.
Both may be given together.
A run with none of those three options is a usage error.
.PP
The program never writes to PostgreSQL or to the data directory.
Online mode runs only SELECT queries, in a read-only session.
A DSN that contains a password is refused.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --json
Print the report as JSON.
.TP
.B --datadir \fIPATH\fR
Read this PostgreSQL data directory (offline checks).
.TP
.B --dsn \fIDSN\fR
Also run the online checks through psql -d DSN.
Only SELECT queries run, in a read-only session.
A DSN with a password is refused: use ~/.pgpass or PGPASSWORD.
.TP
.B --online
Run the online checks with the libpq environment (PGHOST, PGUSER, ...) only.
.TP
.B "-h, --help"
Print help.
.TP
.B "-V, --version"
Print version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Nothing actionable: no finding is Warn, NeedsRoot, or Error.
.B --help
and
.B --version
also exit 0.
.TP
.B 1
A check reported Warn, NeedsRoot, or Error.
A refused DSN and a failing connection are Error findings.
A
.B --datadir
that is not a data directory (no
.I PG_VERSION
or no
.IR pg_wal )
is an Error finding too, so it exits 1.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error: an unknown option, or none of
.BR --datadir ,
.BR --dsn ,
or
.BR --online .
.SH EXAMPLES
From the repository root, read the fictional data directory
.I examples/quiet-datadir
(one invented 24-hex segment name, one
.I .done
marker, and no
.I .ready
file).
Expected exit code 0:
.PP
.nf
pgwal-doctor --datadir examples/quiet-datadir
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PGWAL_DOCTOR_PSQL
Program to run instead of
.I psql
for online checks.
.TP
.B PGHOST, PGUSER, ...
Libpq connection settings used by
.BR --online ,
and by
.B --dsn
when the DSN does not set them.
.TP
.B PGPASSWORD
Password for online checks.
A password inside
.B --dsn
is refused.
.SH SEE ALSO
.I README.md
in the source tree.
The manual source is
.IR man/pgwal-doctor.1 .
